      "id": "ccna-rest-profile-handover",
      "version": 1,
      "track": "CCNA",
      "topic": "REST network changes",
      "unit": "rest-network-changes",
      "title": "Hand over a controller profile without collateral changes",
      "summary": "Create, rebind, verify and retire resources while protecting another group.",
      "objective": "Move both guest ports (desk-3 and desk-4) to a new working profile in VLAN 30. Keep guest peers connected and separate from staff. Keep the staff profile unchanged. Retire the old visitors profile after moving its bindings.",
      "retry_guidance": "Read the actual response first. Correct the request fields and send again; then use each failing network requirement to check the applied result.",
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "minutes": 30,
      "prerequisites": [
        "ccna-rest-change-request"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Create data before choosing it",
        "Move one binding at a time",
        "Retire safely after verification",
        "Use replacement and partial changes deliberately"
      ],
      "guide": [
        {
          "title": "Create data before choosing it",
          "why": "POST /profiles creates a named profile from name, up and vlan. A 201 response includes Location, the new resource path. PUT /profiles/NAME can also create a full profile at that path. Existing port bindings keep their old selection until you change them.",
          "action": "Use the native request controls and inspect the actual response.",
          "commands": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Move one binding at a time",
          "why": "GET /bindings lists port selections. PATCH /bindings/desk-3 with a new profile name changes only that port. Moving just one peer can split a working pair: a valid 204 response is not a complete handover.",
          "action": "Use the native request controls and inspect the actual response.",
          "commands": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Retire safely after verification",
          "why": "DELETE removes an unused profile. This origin returns 409 while a port still selects it, so read the bindings and move the remaining users first. The two guest ports need the target VLAN; staff must keep its existing profile and behavior.",
          "action": "Use the native request controls and inspect the actual response.",
          "commands": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Use replacement and partial changes deliberately",
          "why": "PUT replaces the whole resource representation; PATCH changes only named fields. PATCH description:null removes an optional description. Removing up, vlan or a binding profile is invalid because those fields are required. You may choose a different new profile name if its behavior meets the full assignment.",
          "action": "Use the native request controls and inspect the actual response.",
          "commands": []
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Creation, port selection and retirement were separate resource operations. Both guest bindings needed a working target profile before their old one could be deleted. Current Ethernet outcomes and preserved staff data mattered more than request order or the chosen new profile name.",
      "hints": [
        "Use GET /profiles and GET /bindings with an empty Body to inspect current resources. The supplied map connects binding names to switch ports and endpoints.",
        "401 means identity missing or invalid; 403 means identified but not permitted; 415 means wrong Content-Type; 400 means a JSON, path or request-format error; 422 means the data violates this resource schema.",
        "A 2xx response is not completion. Check network, read each failing requirement, and keep unrelated profile fields intact."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://learningcontent.cisco.com/documents/marketing/exam-topics/200-301-CCNA-v1.1.pdf",
        "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html",
        "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7396.html"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Sources checked 2026-11-13UTC. Finite in-process lab origin, not a Cisco API or HTTP wire implementation. Supplied synthetic Bearer roles are not real credentials, Basic, OAuth or TLS. Named profiles and fixed access-port bindings project into existing Ethernet/VLAN simulation. GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE only; JSON and Merge Patch with typed resource limits. No URL, server, socket, shell or host execution. Up to12profiles/12bindings,4KiB request bodies,128JSON values/depth8,64changes/16KiB replay and64KiB session. See REST_CONTROLLER_SUBSET.md. No complete6.5or controller architecture claim.",
      "initial": {
        "kind": "RestController",
        "simulation": {
          "version": 1,
          "context": "ccna-rest-profile-handover",
          "view": "introduction",
          "assignment": {
            "request": {
              "method": "GET",
              "path": "/profiles",
              "authorization": "Bearer lab-reader",
              "content_type": "application/json",
              "body": ""
